      "writtenOn": "2022-12-16T06:04:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Then we have the same log in two places. I don\u0027t think that\u0027s what most people will want. They would rather have an option to consume logs by themselves, or redirect them to the system (logd).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 479,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 480,
        "endChar": 58
      },
      "revId": "a9cf83bfada08ff53e961852106c1650c89c3239",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e50d905e_7bf7c2fd",
        "filename": "virtualizationservice/src/aidl.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 480,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-16T10:13:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Then we have the same log in two places. I don\u0027t think that\u0027s what most people will want. \n\nAgreed.\n\nFWIW the Java API currently always passes in fds for console \u0026 log output.\nBut it is up to clients whether they read from those fds, and if so what they do with them.\nWhich I suspect means that if they choose to ignore the output fd, the loop below will quite quickly end up blocked in file.write_all().\n(Will that then cause problems further upstream?)",
      "parentUuid": "d1c6d8d6_27408efc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 479,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 480,
        "endChar": 58
      },
      "revId": "a9cf83bfada08ff53e961852106c1650c89c3239",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f6b1cc45_36dccf4f",
        "filename": "virtualizationservice/src/aidl.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 480,
      "author": {
        "id": 1291338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-19T09:39:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e \u003eThen we have the same log in two places. I don\u0027t think that\u0027s what most people will want.\n\u003e\n\u003e Agreed.\n\nHmm, why? Although I understand your point, there are logs printed to more than one place. e.g. adb logcat and dmesg share some logs.\n\n\u003e But it is up to clients whether they read from those fds, and if so what they do with them.\n\nIt sounds like we should change the API by adding `VirtualMachine.setConsole(fd)` to give users a choice, like:\n\n    VirtualMachine vm \u003d VirtualMachineManager.getOrCreate(config);\n    ParcelFileDescriptor[] pipe \u003d ParcelFileDescriptor.createPipe();\n    vm.setConsole(pipe[1]);\n    vm.run();\n    \n    while (read from pipe[0]) {\n        // do whatever..\n    }\n    \nso, if `setConsole` isn\u0027t called, it\u0027s forwarded to `logd` by `virtualizationservice`. If we want this way, we may want to refactor functions like `createVmPipes`, `getConsoleOutput`, etc. Is it what we want?",
      "parentUuid": "e50d905e_7bf7c2fd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 479,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 480,
        "endChar": 58
      },
      "revId": "a9cf83bfada08ff53e961852106c1650c89c3239",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7caeb11a_a84fc9a6",
        "filename": "virtualizationservice/src/aidl.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 480,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-19T11:06:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From the perspective of the app who owns a VM, the logs from the VM are not much different from logs from the host VM (the ones generated by the app itself, framework, and the system servers on behalf of the app). App doesn\u0027t expect to read logs back because most of the logs must have been produced by itself.\n\nSo, I think the most preferred option is that:\n\n(1) VM logs, by default, go to the host-side logd.\n(2) they could be redirected to the owning app if the app for some reason doesn\u0027t want to share the logs with others, but wants to have the logs for diagnostics purpose.\n\n\u003e we should change the API by adding VirtualMachine.setConsole(fd)\n\nWe could. But a simpler option might be adding methods like `VirtualMachineConfig.Builder.setRedirectConsoleOutputToApp(boolean)` so that users don\u0027t have to create the pipe, but use the existing method `getConsoleOutput()`.",
      "parentUuid": "f6b1cc45_36dccf4f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 479,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 480,
        "endChar": 58
      },
      "revId": "a9cf83bfada08ff53e961852106c1650c89c3239",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
